<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH POWER FIRM 1996 AUDITED NET RISES.</title>
<headline>CZECH POWER FIRM 1996 AUDITED NET RISES.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech regional power distributor Vychodoceska Energetika a.s. said on Friday its net profit in 1996 rose to 335 million crowns from 326 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Audited results for year ending December 31, 1996 (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Net profit		  335.01     vs	   326.04</p>
<p> Gross profit		413.56     vs	   529.65</p>
<p> Operating profit	  355.51     vs	   528.79</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services	    8,104.85     vs	 7,622.25</p>
<p> Total assets	    6,904.21     vs	 6,367.46</p>
<p> Basic capital	   2,473.97     vs	 2,473.97</p>
<p>NOTE: The company is a regional electricity distributor based in the central city of Hradec Kralove. Its shares are listed on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. The results are according to Czech accounting standards.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
